From: mscharged-port
Subject: Address the MSL format cursor where va_list is a struct (AArch64)
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84
Classification: native compiler/ABI compatibility.

0678 passes parse_format the address of __wpformatter's va_list cursor: the
parameter itself on x86-64 (array va_list) and its address on Apple arm64
(pointer va_list). On AArch64 Linux and the Nintendo Switch va_list is a
struct, and the branch that casts the parameter to a pointer no longer
compiles, as both branches of a non-template if constexpr are checked. A
template lambda compiles only the branch the native va_list takes: the same
two expressions on x86-64 and Apple arm64, the parameter's address on AArch64.

diff --git a/src/MSL/wprintf.c b/src/MSL/wprintf.c
index 2b63501..f2312ad 100644
--- a/src/MSL/wprintf.c
+++ b/src/MSL/wprintf.c
@@ -1040,13 +1040,17 @@ int __wpformatter(void* (*WriteProc)(void*, const wchar_t*, size_t), void* Write
 
         format_ptr = curr_format;
 #if defined(MSCHARGED_NATIVE) && defined(__cplusplus)
-        // Pointer-shaped va_list addresses the local cursor. An array-shaped
-        // function parameter already carries the underlying cursor by address.
-        if constexpr (__is_same(va_list, decltype(arg))) {
-            format_ptr = parse_format(format_ptr, (va_list*)&arg, &format);
-        } else {
-            format_ptr = parse_format(format_ptr, (va_list*)arg, &format);
-        }
+        // Pointer-shaped (Apple arm64) and struct-shaped (AArch64 AAPCS)
+        // va_list address the local cursor. An array-shaped function parameter
+        // (x86-64) already carries the underlying cursor by address. A template
+        // compiles only the branch the native va_list takes.
+        format_ptr = parse_format(format_ptr, []<class Cursor>(Cursor& cursor) -> va_list* {
+            if constexpr (__is_same(Cursor, va_list)) {
+                return &cursor;
+            } else {
+                return (va_list*)cursor;
+            }
+        }(arg), &format);
 #else
         format_ptr = parse_format(format_ptr, (va_list*)arg, &format);
 #endif
